[{:seon.task/name "an-agent-follows-its-instructions-to-green"
  :seon.task/plan "The owner, 2026-10-30: deliver improved context, tested with DeepSeek agents on whether they follow their instructions. Measured on the md-scan bench (task seon.ref/markdown-reads-the-scan, deepseek-flash, a 40-turn cap; stores in .worktrees/ctx-ui-review, mains bench-30 to bench-34, and .worktrees/bench-b, mains bench-b1 to bench-b12): 0 green of 5 before task seon.context/the-page-is-the-render-of-what-ctx-pulls, 1 of 5 after it (B1, 36 turns), 0 of 5 once a broken parser reached the model; every other run at the cap. An audit of those runs and of bench-b10's first request (6.6k tokens) found six causes, each now fixed:
1. The instructions conflicted (reproduce first, beside red proofs shown with their source). Fixed: :work and :whole share `seon.template/work-steps`: red proofs with their source are the reproduction, so make the first change; only a fix with no failing proof is reproduced first; a long definition is changed by edit!; each change is checked with the proof's own expression (B1, the green run, did). 1,640 -> 1,250 characters, so :whole is drawn whole within the 600-token value budget.
2. Progress was invisible. Fixed: the run head reads turn N of its cap and K changes (`seon.render.ui/run-head`); three of five runs changed nothing in 40 turns.
3. The var the task changes showed only its read form, so every run read scan and markdown at turn 0. Fixed: a cited var of the task's own namespaces shows its source at doc depth (`seon.render.ui/cite-model`).
4. Noise, about 4.4k of the first request's 6.6k tokens. Fixed: a proof's callees are named only (their docstrings were about 2.4k), markdown's regex test names only the regex functions it found (not about 60 clojure.core symbols), and :to-prove lists only unwritten proofs.
5. A stray red showed its failures only (bench-b11 ended on 11 it could not trace). Fixed: it carries its source and calls, as a red proof does (`seon.context/status`).
6. Every eval threw once the agent broke scan (bench-b8): the eval path parsed each call's prose with the agent's parser. Fixed at its cause (`seon.repl/record-details` parses nothing; `my.agent/no-var` names a parser's throw).
Items 1-5 merged from jolt/follow, item 6 in batch 56 (f33343d9ca). Left: the measure, the same bench, five runs on main, each run's turns to green, its first request's tokens beside bench-b10's 6.6k, and whether it took the first change when red proofs showed their source."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.template-test/red-proofs-with-their-source-are-the-reproduction seon.context-test/the-run-head-shows-what-the-branch-changed
