  {:seon.task/name "the-turn-shows-what-will-merge"
  :seon.task/plan "Done: `seon.merge/divergence` names the vars the branch added, redefined and removed and the schema keys it registered or changed (from each db's :var/form and :schema/form datoms; `seon.merge/changed-vars` is its vars); `seon.turn/observe` takes it against the agent's `:base` (`seon.agent/state`), its branch's merge base with main, set at init and by `seon.agent/merge-main!` after each merge (and for a resumed branch), and `seon.context/current-state` shows it as `:will-merge` among the turn sections (DECISIONS: D4). The merge base, not the main the agent forked from: against that, a branch cut before main changed a function showed main's change as its own. Not covered: data entities a branch writes (`seon.merge/program`'s :datum keys) and multimethod and protocol definitions, which only the full program merge sees (`seon.merge/program`, 440 ms per db, too slow for every turn)."
