 {:seon.task/name "an-unrun-proof-is-unknown-in-the-context"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `seon.context/current-state` (context.clj, the `:proofs` entry: `(get results p (cond (nil? src) :undefined (seq test-run-errors) :not-run :else :no-assertions))`) labels a proof that is written but has no result :no-assertions, and docs/agent.md#what-you-read tells the agent that means it ran and asserted nothing. A result is absent whenever no report named the test (`seon.agent/run-tests-forked`): one not selected or not loaded as well as one with no assertion. Root's judge reads the same absence as :proof-unknown (`seon.reconcile/done-explain`, reconcile.clj), so agent and judge disagree on one fact. Reproduction (audit): 263 of 265 contexts showed every proof :no-assertions while none had run; agents then loosened a contract. Correct: the status is :unknown. Write set: that `cond` default in `current-state`; the :no-assertions sentence in docs/agent.md (the `:proofs` bullet of the turn's part). Deletes the :no-assertions default. Red now: `bin/test seon.context-test` fails `a-proof-with-no-result-reads-unknown`, and `a-failure-reads-as-assert-and-got`, whose old line asserting :no-assertions is changed to :unknown."
